.SH NAME
CWE\-664 \- Improper Control of a Resource Through its Lifetime
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product does not maintain or incorrectly maintains control over a resource throughout its lifetime of creation, use, and release. Resources often have explicit instructions on how to be created, used and destroyed. When code does not follow these instructions, it can lead to unexpected behaviors and potentially exploitable states. Even without explicit instructions, various principles are expected to be adhered to, such as Do not use an object until after its creation is complete, or do not use an object after it has been slated for destruction.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2022\-27518
Citrix Application Delivery Controller (ADC) and Gateway, added 2022\-12\-13.
.PP
Citrix Application Delivery Controller (ADC) and Gateway Authentication Bypass Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Citrix Application Delivery Controller (ADC) and Gateway, when configured with SAML SP or IdP configuration, contain an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows an attacker to execute code as administrator.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2023\-01\-03.
.PP
